.\" pg_improv(7): the SQL API and GUCs, condensed from crates/pg_improv/README.md.
.TH PG_IMPROV 7 "" "improv" "Improv Manual"
.SH NAME
pg_improv \- Improv's incremental modeling engine as a Postgres extension
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
CREATE EXTENSION pg_improv;
SELECT improv.create_model(\(aqplan\(aq);
SELECT improv.bind_category(\(aqplan\(aq, \(aqTime\(aq, \(aqsales\(aq, \(aqyear\(aq);
SELECT improv.bind_measure(\(aqplan\(aq, \(aqPrice\(aq, \(aqsales\(aq, \(aqprice\(aq, \(aqmax\(aq);
SELECT improv.define(\(aqplan\(aq, \(aqRevenue = Price * Quantity\(aq);
SELECT * FROM improv_plan.revenue;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pg_improv
binds table columns to Improv categories and measures, defines derived
measures in Improv's formula language
.RB ( improv-formulas (7)),
and keeps their results in ordinary tables,
.BI improv_ model . measure\fR,
with one
.B text
column per dimension, a typed
.B value
column and a primary key on the dimensions. It supports Postgres 15 to 18.
Every function is in schema
.B improv
and is
.BR "SECURITY INVOKER" ;
.B CREATE EXTENSION
needs a superuser.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.BI create_model( name )
Create a model and its result schema
.BI improv_ name\fR.
.TP
.BI bind_category( model ", " category ", " rel ", " col )
Record that
.IB rel . col
supplies the category's items.
.TP
.BI bind_measure( model ", " measure ", " rel ", " value_col " [, " agg ])
An input measure read from
.IB rel . value_col\fR,
over the categories bound on
.IR rel .
Two rows on one coordinate are an error unless
.I agg
.RB ( sum ,
.BR avg ,
.BR min ,
.BR max ,
.BR count ,
.BR count_distinct )
folds them.
.TP
.BI define( model ", " definition " [, " replace ])
A derived measure from
.IR "Target = expr" ,
or a named LAMBDA. An existing name is an error unless
.I replace
is true; an unchanged formula is then a no-op.
.TP
.BI drop_measure( model ", " measure )
Drop a measure or LAMBDA; an error names what still uses it.
.TP
.BI recalc( model " [, " measures ])
Recompute (the named measures and their dependents) in the caller's
transaction; returns the rows changed.
.TP
.BI set_sync_mode( model ", " mode )
.B logical
(the default),
.BR trigger ,
.B commit
or
.BR manual .
.TP
.BI what_if( model ", " edits )
The derived cells that
.I edits
(jsonb) would change, computed in memory; writes nothing.
.TP
.BI status( model )
The sync mode, the logical worker's slot and lag, and its last error.
.TP
.BI enable_logical( model "), sync_publication()"
Maintain the publication
.B improv_db
(called for you).
.TP
.BI drop_model( name )
Drop the model, its result schema and its triggers.
.SH SYNC MODES
.TP
.B logical
A background worker tails a logical replication slot and applies each
batch of committed changes in one transaction, shortly after the commit.
Needs
.B shared_preload_libraries = \(aqpg_improv\(aq
and
.BR wal_level=logical .
.TP
.B trigger
Statement triggers recompute in the writer's statement: read-your-writes.
.TP
.B commit
Recompute once per writing transaction, just before it commits.
.TP
.B manual
Only
.B improv.recalc
updates results.
.SH LANGUAGE improv
.nf
CREATE FUNCTION margin(price float8, cost float8) RETURNS float8
  LANGUAGE improv IMMUTABLE AS $$ price \- cost $$;
.fi
.PP
A function body is Improv formulas over the named arguments; the last line
is the result. A NULL argument is a missing input, and an error value
returns NULL (or raises, with
.BR improv.raise_errors ).
The language is trusted.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.BR improv.database " (string, default " postgres ", postmaster)"
The database the sync worker serves. Registered only when the library is
preloaded.
.TP
.BR improv.poll_ms " (integer, default 200, 10 to 60000, sighup)"
How often the sync worker polls its slot, in milliseconds.
.TP
.BR improv.max_changes " (integer, default 10000, sighup)"
The most decoded changes one poll reads.
.TP
.BR improv.max_cells " (integer, default 5000000, user)"
The most bound input cells
.B recalc
loads; above it, it raises an error.
.TP
.BR improv.raise_errors " (boolean, default off, user)"
Make a
.B LANGUAGE improv
function whose result is an error value raise it instead of returning NULL.
.PP
Set
.B max_slot_wal_keep_size
to cap the WAL a stuck worker can retain.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR improv (1),
.BR improv-formulas (7),
.BR improv-functions (7).
The full reference: crates/pg_improv/README.md, or Improv in Postgres in
the user guide, https://gregburd.codeberg.page/improv/.
